  "rules": {
    "S": "S(arm) = #cells where the donor-new-source patch is JOINT and the donor-ROUND-source patch of the same arm is not (target host new)",
    "SPEC": "SPEC iff dM_main > dM_round in >= 75% of cells AND in a majority of cells for >= 10 of 14 donor groups",
    "always_reported": "S, SPEC, J_main, J_round and median dM per arm; alpha statistics per dir arm; per-cell ||delta_C|| and cos(delta_C, delta_full) from the capture files; leave-one-donor-group-out of every verdict; per host; all nulls",
    "bulk_rules": "BULK_SUF iff S(only_BULK) >= 1/2 S(full) and SPEC(only_BULK); BULK_NEC iff S(drop_BULK) <= 1/2 S(full)",
    "consistency_gate": "the full arm is the M3 all-heads patch: its 208 rows must equal M3's bitwise (GPU, checked in the run) and S(full) = 51; otherwise verdict INCONSISTENT_WITH_M3 and no claim",
    "content_rule": "XD_HOLDS iff S(xdonor_BULK) >= 1/2 S(full) and SPEC(xdonor_BULK): the BULK part need not come from the same scene as the rest of the donor's write; else XD_FAILS",
    "direction_rules": "DIR_SUF(C) iff S(dir_C) >= 1/2 S(full) and SPEC(dir_C), for C in PARTNER, ROUND_PEERS, OTHER_ITEMS, CONTEXT, SELF, ROUNDVOTES, BULK. RAND_NULL iff S(dir_RAND) <= 5 and not SPEC(dir_RAND)",
    "interpretation_fixed_in_advance": "M4's necessity of OTHER_ITEMS / CONTEXT is a size effect if RAND_NULL holds and BULK_DIRECTION does not, or if a non-BULK class repairs at matched size (PARTNER_DIRECTION: the partner direction carries the evaluation and was only too small in M4). BULK_DIRECTION with RAND_NULL: the context-wide read carries the round-specific evaluation in its direction, not only its size. NO_SINGLE_DIRECTION: the evaluation is a combination across classes. dir_C rescales a direction by a position-wise factor alpha_C that can be large; alpha statistics are always reported. All keys before the span are identical in a scene's new and ROUND arms, so round-specificity of pre-span classes comes from the donor's span-side queries and gates (the round token is at the span end)",
    "matched_size_gate": "for every dir_* and dir_RAND row, the patch's change ||patch - host|| per row and span position equals ||donor - host|| within 1e-3 relative (fail-closed in the runner)",
    "readouts": "M = conflict margin; A = logit(reject_conflict) - max(accept, wait); JOINT = M > 0 and A > 0; dM = M(patch) - M(in-run capture of host new)",
    "units": "the 104 cross-group cells of M1-M4; cells share donors and hosts, counts are descriptive decision rules, not independent tests",
    "verdict": "if not RAND_NULL: MAGNITUDE_SUFFICES (a random direction at the full patch's size repairs; no direction claim). Else D = {C : DIR_SUF(C)}: PARTNER_DIRECTION if PARTNER or ROUNDVOTES in D and no BULK-side class (OTHER_ITEMS, CONTEXT, BULK) in D; BULK_DIRECTION if a BULK-side class in D and neither PARTNER nor ROUNDVOTES in D; BOTH_DIRECTIONS if both kinds in D; SELF_DIRECTION if D = {SELF}; NO_SINGLE_DIRECTION if D is empty (the repair needs the donor's write as a whole)"
  },
